.TH SLACKRESOLVE 8 "2026-11-08" "SlackResolve 0.3.3"
.SH NAME
slackresolve \- find and install missing Slackware ELF dependencies
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B slackresolve check-program
PROGRAM [--output PLAN] [options]
.br
.B slackresolve search-file
FILE [--output PLAN] [options]
.br
.B slackresolve check-system
[--output PLAN] [options]
.br
.B slackresolve install
PACKAGE|ARCHIVE [--output PLAN] [options]
.br
.B slackresolve show
PLAN
.br
.B slackresolve apply
PLAN [--dry-run]
.br
.B slackresolve verify
PLAN
.SH DESCRIPTION
SlackResolve locates exact filenames or package paths, examines dynamic ELF requirements, searches official Slackware package contents through slackpkg, follows provider dependencies recursively, and saves exact package archives in a reviewable plan.
.PP
Planning never installs packages. Applying a ready plan uses installpkg for additions and upgradepkg for replacements. Installed ELF consumers are checked before an upgrade is approved. Parallel package versions are accepted only when their files and library identities do not conflict.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --arch ARCH
Override target package architecture detection for an incomplete alternate root.
.TP
.BI --repo " DIR|slackpkg"
Use a local package tree or the official indexes configured for slackpkg.
.TP
.BI --output " FILE"
Save a plan and its adjacent FILE.d archive directory.
.TP
.BI --root " DIR"
Analyze a target root instead of /.
.TP
.BI --cache " DIR"
Use an alternate analysis cache.
.TP
.BI --prefer " NAME[,NAME]"
Prefer named packages when several compatible providers exist.
.TP
.B --dry-run
Validate and print apply operations without modifying the target.
.SH FILES
.I /var/lib/pkgtools/packages
installed package records.
.br
.I /var/lib/slackpkg
official slackpkg indexes.
.br
.I /var/cache/packages
archives downloaded by slackpkg.
.SH SEE ALSO
slackpkg(8), installpkg(8), upgradepkg(8), ldconfig(8), readelf(1), dialog(1)
